ise calculation confirms the initial observation: borrowing reached 113.6% of the deficit, significantly higher than the previous year's 90.8%. This suggests substantial changes in fiscal financing between the two periods, indicating a notable shift in how the government managed its financial resources during this timeframe.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_f6f9ed6ff90d4db8a122b745","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\n# Q1 FY1990\ndeficit_1990 = 69688\nborrowing_1990 = 63300\nshare_1990 = (borrowing_1990 / deficit_1990) * 100\nprint(f'Q1 FY1990: ({borrowing_1990} / {deficit_1990}) * 100 = {share_1990:.2f}%')\n\n# Q1 FY1991\ndeficit_1991 = 86898\nborrowing_1991 = 98741\nshare_1991 = (borrowing_1991 / deficit_1991) * 100\nprint(f'Q1 FY1991: ({borrowing_1991} / {deficit_1991}) * 100 = {share_1991:.2f}%')\n\n# Absolute difference\ndiff = abs(share_1991 - share_1990)\nprint(f'Absolute difference: {diff:.2f} percentage points')\n\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
